==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|leggja}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*lagjaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈlɛcːa/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɛcːa|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|lagði|lagt}}

# to [[lay]], to [[put]] {{+obj|is|acc}}
#: {{syn|is|láta}}
#: {{ux|is|'''Leggðu''' bókina niður.|'''Put''' the book down.}}
# to [[lay]] (stones, tiles, a road), to [[pave]] {{+obj|is|acc}}
#: {{syn|is|byggja}}
#: {{ux|is|Að '''leggja''' hellur.|To '''pave'''.}}
#: {{ux|is|Að '''leggja''' veg.|To '''pave''' a road.}}
# to [[jab]], [[thrust]] {{+obj|is|acc}}
#: {{syn|is|stinga}}
# to [[park]] (a [[vehicle]]) {{+obj|is|&intransitive/dat}}
#: {{syn|is|parkera}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég kann ekki að '''leggja'''.|I don't know how to '''park'''.}}
#: {{ux|is|Hvernig gekk að '''leggja''' bílnum?|How did '''parking''' the car go?}}
# {{lb|is|impersonal}} to [[cause]] to become [[cover]]ed in [[ice]], to [[cause]] to [[freeze over]] {{+obj|is|dat<something>}} {{q|idiomatically translated as "become covered with ice, freeze over" with the dative object as the subject}}
#: {{ux|is|Tjörnina '''lagði'''.|The lake '''froze over'''.}}
# {{lb|is|impersonal|of smoke, smell, etc.}} to [[waft]] (over an area, room, etc.)
# {{lb|is|impersonal}} to [[cause]] to [[waft]], to [[cause]] to [[fill]] {{+obj|is|acc<smoke, a smell, etc.> + :um(acc)<(over) an area, room, etc.>}} {{q|idiomatically translated as "waft over" or "fill" with the accusative object as the subject}}
#: {{ux|is|Reykinn '''lagði''' um húsið.|The smoke '''filled''' the house.}}

